From b111507fb0bf686f55a3443de6f8deb4f30753c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 31/45] Project PDF for v2.0.0-NAS

Built by tools/nas-kit/doc/build_pdf.py from project.md, the folder's git
history (change history) and its code (listings), so it names the release it
describes. Section 9, "Keeping up with upstream: what each release changed",
lists for every port from v1.20.5 to v2.0.0 what stopped the patches and how
it was resolved. Section 3 explains the relay's discovery fix (answers from
the arrival interface, so the NAS's VPN client no longer hides it); the
verification table and the sources are up to date, including RTTY over the
NAS (new in upstream v2.0.0, not yet tried).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
